# Skill: feature-tester

Read and follow `skills/feature-builder/feature-tester/SKILL.md`. Fill `skills/feature-builder/feature-tester/assets/what-was-verified.md` only.

Announce: `Using skill: feature-tester`.

## Job

Prove the implementation matches `what-to-build.md`. Write real tests, run the commands this repo already has, report pass/fail. This is not code review (`feature-code-reviewer`).

## Must (order)

1. Read `what-to-build.md` and the shipped code.
2. Add tests for done-when, no-path, leave/cancel, and at least one wall. No hollow asserts.
3. Find the commands via `package.json` scripts, `Makefile`, `pyproject.toml` / `tox.ini` / `noxfile.py`, CI workflows, then the README. Run unit, integration, e2e, and security. If a layer does not exist, write `absent`. If Playwright / `test:e2e` exists, run it for UI work. Do not invent CI or a framework.
4. Write `agent-engineer-skills/<name>/what-was-verified.md`. Verdicts are `pass`, `fail`, `not-run`.

An e2e run that fails on a missing precondition (no dev server, browsers not installed) is `not-run` with a reason, never `fail`. Windows PowerShell 5.1 has no `&&` operator; run commands one per call there.

## Must not

- New product
- New test runner, CI, or scanner vendor
- Threat-model essay
- Claim pass without a command result or a repeatable manual check
